[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me provide a comprehensive report.\n\n## Daemon Build Setup - Comprehensive Analysis\n\n### 1. Daemon Package Structure\n\nThe daemon is located at `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/daemon/` with the following structure:\n\n```\npackages/daemon/\n├── package.json                    # Daemon package manifest\n├── tsconfig.json                   # TypeScript configuration\n├── src/\n│   ├── index.ts                    # Entry point (#!/usr/bin/env bun shebang)\n│   ├── server.ts                   # Elysia.js HTTP server setup\n│   ├── pid.ts                      # PID file management\n│   ├── project-context.ts          # Multi-project context manager\n│   ├── watcher.ts                  # File watcher (Bun fs.watch + Chokidar fallback)\n│   ├── middleware/\n│   │   └── project-context.ts      # Elysia middleware for project binding\n│   ├── routes/\n│   │   ├── tasks.ts                # Task API endpoints\n│   │   ├── items.ts                # Spec item API endpoints\n│   │   ├── inbox.ts                # Inbox API endpoints\n│   │   ├── meta.ts                 # Meta/session API endpoints\n│   │   ├── validation.ts           # Search/validation API endpoints\n│   │   └── projects.ts             # Project management endpoints\n│   └── websocket/\n│       ├── pubsub.ts               # Pub/Sub manager\n│       ├── handler.ts              # WebSocket message handler\n│       ├── heartbeat.ts            # Heartbeat monitoring\n│       └── types.ts                # TypeSocket types\n└── dist/\n    └── kspec-daemon                # Compiled standalone executable (from bun build --compile)\n```\n\n### 2. Package.json Configuration\n\n**daemon/package.json:**\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"@kynetic-ai/daemon\",\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"main\": \"dist/index.js\",\n  \"bin\": {\n    \"kspec-daemon\": \"./dist/index.js\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"tsc\",\n    \"build:compile\": \"bun build --compile --minify src/index.ts --outfile dist/kspec-daemon\",\n    \"dev\": \"bun --watch src/index.ts\",\n    \"start\": \"bun dist/index.js\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@elysiajs/cors\": \"^1.1.3\",\n    \"@elysiajs/static\": \"^1.4.7\",\n    \"@kynetic-ai/shared\": \"*\",\n    \"chokidar\": \"^4.0.3\",\n    \"elysia\": \"^1.1.31\",\n    \"ulidx\": \"^2.4.1\",\n    \"yaml\": \"^2.7.0\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@types/bun\": \"latest\",\n    \"typescript\": \"^5.3.3\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nKey features:\n- **build:compile**: Produces a standalone executable with `bun build --compile --minify`\n- **Entry point**: `./dist/index.js` (after TypeScript compilation)\n- **Cross-package dependency**: `@kynetic-ai/shared` using monorepo workspace wildcard\n\n### 3. Bun Build --Compile Command\n\n**Command from daemon/package.json:**\n```bash\nbun build --compile --minify src/index.ts --outfile dist/kspec-daemon\n```\n\n**Extended script from scripts/build-executables.sh** (for cross-platform builds):\n```bash\n# Supports multiple platforms:\nbun build --compile --minify --target=bun-linux-x64 packages/daemon/src/index.ts --outfile dist/executables/kspec-daemon-linux-x64\nbun build --compile --minify --target=bun-darwin-arm64 packages/daemon/src/index.ts --outfile dist/executables/kspec-daemon-darwin-arm64\nbun build --compile --minify --target=bun-darwin-x64 packages/daemon/src/index.ts --outfile dist/executables/kspec-daemon-darwin-x64\nbun build --compile --minify --target=bun-windows-x64 packages/daemon/src/index.ts --outfile dist/executables/kspec-daemon-win-x64.exe\n```\n\nThe executable is **100% standalone** - runs without Bun runtime. The `--minify` flag removes whitespace/comments. Target flags enable cross-compilation.\n\n### 4. Test File: tests/daemon-executable.test.ts\n\nThis test file validates the executable compilation process:\n\n**What it tests:**\n1. **Compilation success**: Runs `bun run build:compile` from daemon directory with 60-second timeout\n2. **Executable exists**: Verifies file is created at expected path (handles both `dist/kspec-daemon` and `packages/daemon/dist/kspec-daemon`)\n3. **Execute permissions**: Checks execute bit is set (mode & 0o111 > 0)\n4. **Binary format**: Uses `file` command to verify it's recognized as executable\n5. **Runtime validation**: Runs executable with `--port 9999` flag, verifies it:\n   - Doesn't require Bun (`ENOENT` means failure)\n   - Starts (outputs contain \"daemon\")\n6. **Script presence**: Verifies `build:compile` is in daemon/package.json\n\n**Key fixture paths it handles:**\n```typescript\nconst possiblePaths = [\n  join(process.cwd(), 'dist/kspec-daemon'),\n  join(daemonDir, 'dist/kspec-daemon'),\n];\n```\n\n**Why it matters**: The test has a note that \"bun seems to resolve it from the repo root\" - this addresses ambiguity in whether the compiled output goes to root `dist/` or package `dist/`.\n\n### 5. Cross-Package Relative Imports (Routes)\n\nAll route files use **relative path imports** to access code from the root project. This is the critical issue:\n\n**Pattern: `../../parser/index.js` from `packages/daemon/src/routes/`**\n\n- **tasks.ts** imports from `../../parser/index.js`:\n  ```typescript\n  import {\n    initContext,\n    loadAllTasks,\n    loadAllItems,\n    ReferenceIndex,\n    createNote,\n    saveTask,\n    getAuthor,\n    syncSpecImplementationStatus,\n    type LoadedTask,\n  } from '../../parser/index.js';\n  import { commitIfShadow } from '../../parser/shadow.js';\n  ```\n\n- **items.ts** imports from `../../parser/index.js`:\n  ```typescript\n  import {\n    initContext,\n    loadAllItems,\n    loadAllTasks,\n    ReferenceIndex,\n    AlignmentIndex,\n    getCachedTestCoverage,\n    computeACCoverage,\n    type LoadedSpecItem,\n  } from '../../parser/index.js';\n  ```\n\n- **meta.ts** imports from `../../parser/index.js`:\n  ```typescript\n  import {\n    initContext,\n    loadMetaContext,\n    loadSessionContext,\n  } from '../../parser/index.js';\n  ```\n\n- **validation.ts** imports from both **parser AND utils**:\n  ```typescript\n  import {\n    initContext,\n    buildIndexes,\n    loadInboxItems,\n    loadMetaContext,\n    validate,\n    AlignmentIndex,\n    type LoadedSpecItem,\n    type LoadedTask,\n    type LoadedInboxItem,\n  } from '../../parser/index.js';\n  import type {\n    LoadedAgent,\n    LoadedWorkflow,\n    LoadedObservation,\n    LoadedConvention,\n  } from '../../parser/meta.js';\n  import { grepItem } from '../../utils/grep.js';\n  ```\n\n- **inbox.ts** imports from `../../parser/index.js`:\n  ```typescript\n  import {\n    initContext,\n    loadInboxItems,\n    createInboxItem,\n    saveInboxItem,\n    deleteInboxItem,\n    findInboxItemByRef,\n    ReferenceIndex,\n    loadAllTasks,\n    loadAllItems,\n    type InboxItemInput,\n  } from '../../parser/index.js';\n  import { commitIfShadow } from '../../parser/shadow.js';\n  ```\n\n**Problem**: When `bun build --compile` bundles the daemon, these relative paths require the `src/parser/` and `src/utils/` directories to exist at the **same relative paths** in the final bundle. The build process (`src/` → `dist/daemon/`) preserves these but requires careful path resolution.\n\n### 6. Main Entry Point: packages/daemon/src/index.ts\n\n```typescript\n#!/usr/bin/env bun\n/**\n * Kspec Daemon Entry Point\n * \n * Long-running server that exposes kspec state via HTTP API and WebSocket.\n * Supports foreground and background modes with PID file management.\n * AC: @daemon-server ac-9\n */\n\nimport { createServer } from './server.js';\nimport { parseArgs } from 'util';\nimport { join } from 'path';\n\n// Parse command line args\nconst { values } = parseArgs({\n  args: process.argv.slice(2),\n  options: {\n    port: { type: 'string', default: '3456' },\n    'kspec-dir': { type: 'string' }\n  },\n  allowPositionals: true\n});\n\nconst port = parseInt(values.port as string, 10);\nconst kspecDir = (values['kspec-dir'] as string) || join(process.cwd(), '.kspec');\n\nasync function main() {\n  try {\n    console.log(`[daemon] Starting kspec daemon on port ${port}...`);\n    const server = await createServer({\n      port,\n      isDaemon: true,\n      kspecDir\n    });\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error('[daemon] Failed to start:', error);\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n}\n\nmain();\n```\n\n**Key points:**\n- Shebang `#!/usr/bin/env bun` allows direct execution on Unix systems\n- Accepts `--port` (default 3456) and `--kspec-dir` arguments\n- Delegates to `createServer()` with `isDaemon: true`\n- No explicit port/URL listening log—that happens in server.ts\n\n### 7. Server Setup: packages/daemon/src/server.ts\n\n**createServer() function** (404 lines):\n\n1. **Port/Directory Setup**:\n   - Default port: 3456\n   - Default kspecDir: `.kspec` in process.cwd()\n   - Derives startup project path (parent of `.kspec`)\n\n2. **Initialization Chain**:\n   ```typescript\n   - PidFileManager() → writes ~/.config/kspec/daemon.pid and daemon.port\n   - PubSubManager() → WebSocket pub/sub\n   - HeartbeatManager() → periodic ping/pong checks\n   - WebSocketHandler() → message routing\n   - ProjectContextManager() → multi-project support\n   ```\n\n3. **Elysia.js Setup**:\n   ```typescript\n   const app = new Elysia()\n     .use(cors(...))                              // CORS for localhost:5173\n     .onRequest(localhostOnly())                  // Reject non-localhost\n     .use(projectContextMiddleware(...))          // X-Kspec-Dir extraction\n     .get('/api/health', ...)                     // Health check\n     .use(createTasksRoutes(...))                 // Task API\n     .use(createItemsRoutes(...))                 // Item API\n     .use(createInboxRoutes(...))                 // Inbox API\n     .use(createMetaRoutes(...))                  // Meta API\n     .use(createValidationRoutes(...))            // Validation API\n     .use(createProjectsRoutes(...))              // Projects API\n     .ws('/ws', ...)                              // WebSocket endpoint\n     .use(staticPlugin(...))                      // Web UI serving\n   ```\n\n4. **Middleware Features**:\n   - **localhostOnly()**: Enforces 127.0.0.1, ::1, or localhost hostname\n   - **projectContextMiddleware()**: Extracts `X-Kspec-Dir` header, auto-registers projects, stores in `request.projectContext`\n\n5. **WebSocket Binding**:\n   - Supports `X-Kspec-Dir` header OR `?project=` query param\n   - Auto-registers projects on first connection\n   - Stores immutable project path in `ws.data.projectPath`\n   - Broadcasts on `files:updates`, `tasks:updates`, `inbox:updates`, `files:errors`\n\n6. **Graceful Shutdown**:\n   - Handles SIGTERM/SIGINT\n   - Stops all watchers\n   - Closes WebSocket connections\n   - Removes PID files\n\n### 8. Root Package Build Script\n\n**From root package.json:**\n```json\n{\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"tsc && chmod +x dist/cli/index.js && npm run build:daemon && npm run build:plugin\",\n    \"build:daemon\": \"shx rm -rf dist/daemon && shx mkdir -p dist/daemon && shx cp -r packages/daemon/src/* dist/daemon/\",\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**What `npm run build:daemon` does:**\n1. Removes existing `dist/daemon/` directory\n2. Creates fresh `dist/daemon/` directory\n3. **Copies entire `packages/daemon/src/*` to `dist/daemon/`** (TypeScript source files, NOT compiled)\n\n**Why this matters**: \n- The daemon **source files** end up in the root `dist/` alongside compiled root code\n- This enables the relative imports (`../../parser/`, `../../utils/`) to work from the bundled paths\n- When `bun build --compile` runs, it finds these copied source files alongside parser/utils\n\n**Build pipeline:**\n```\n1. tsc                    → Compile root TypeScript (src/ → dist/)\n2. chmod +x dist/cli/index.js\n3. npm run build:daemon   → Copy daemon sources to dist/daemon/\n4. npm run build:plugin   → Process plugin assets\n5. bun build --compile    → Bundle daemon executable (can find ../../parser now)\n```\n\n### 9. File Structure After Root Build\n\nAfter `npm run build`, the root `dist/` contains:\n\n```\ndist/\n├── daemon/                          # Copied from packages/daemon/src/ (TypeScript source!)\n│   ├── index.ts\n│   ├── server.ts\n│   ├── pid.ts\n│   ├── project-context.ts\n│   ├── watcher.ts\n│   ├── middleware/\n│   ├── routes/\n│   │   ├── tasks.ts                 # Contains: import { ... } from '../../parser/index.js'\n│   │   ├── items.ts                 # Contains: import { ... } from '../../parser/index.js'\n│   │   ├── meta.ts                  # Contains: import { ... } from '../../parser/index.js'\n│   │   ├── validation.ts            # Contains: import { ... } from '../../utils/grep.js'\n│   │   ├── inbox.ts\n│   │   └── projects.ts\n│   └── websocket/\n├── parser/                          # Compiled from src/parser/ (JavaScript)\n├── utils/                           # Compiled from src/utils/ (JavaScript)\n├── cli/\n├── lib/\n└── ... (other compiled code)\n```\n\n**Key insight**: The relative imports `../../parser/index.js` resolve correctly because:\n- From `dist/daemon/routes/tasks.ts` → `../../` goes to `dist/`\n- Then `parser/index.js` points to `dist/parser/index.js` (compiled JavaScript)\n- But wait... `dist/daemon/` contains **TypeScript source files**, not compiled JavaScript!\n\n### 10. The Compilation Issue\n\nThis is where things get complex:\n\n**When `bun build --compile src/index.ts` runs:**\n\nIt resolves imports starting from `packages/daemon/src/index.ts` and finds:\n```typescript\nimport { createServer } from './server.js';  // packages/daemon/src/server.ts\n```\n\nThen `server.ts` has:\n```typescript\nimport { createTasksRoutes } from './routes/tasks.js';  // packages/daemon/src/routes/tasks.ts\n```\n\nThen `tasks.ts` has:\n```typescript\nimport { initContext, ... } from '../../parser/index.js';\n```\n\n**Relative path resolution from `packages/daemon/src/routes/tasks.ts`:**\n- `../../` → up 2 levels → `packages/` → then `parser/index.js`? NO!\n- Should go to **project root** `parser/index.js`\n\n**This is the broken path.** The relative imports are expecting to find `parser/` and `utils/` at the project root, but they're resolving from the daemon package subdirectory.\n\n**How it actually works** (or should work with monorepo tooling):\n\n1. **During development** (`npm run dev` or `bun --watch src/index.ts`):\n   - Bun runs from `packages/daemon/`\n   - Imports need to be relative to actual filesystem\n   - Paths like `../../parser/` fail because `packages/parser/` doesn't exist\n   - **The routes aren't actually usable in development from the daemon package!**\n\n2. **During root build** (`npm run build`):\n   - Copies daemon sources to `dist/daemon/`\n   - Compiles root to `dist/` (including parser, utils)\n   - Creates correct relative structure\n\n3. **When bundling** (`bun build --compile`):\n   - Should run from project root with correct path context\n   - OR the build script should handle path rewriting\n\n### Test Failure Analysis (tests/daemon-executable.test.ts)\n\n**The test tries to:**\n```typescript\nconst buildResult = spawnSync('bun', ['run', 'build:compile'], {\n  cwd: daemonDir,  // <-- Running from packages/daemon/\n  encoding: 'utf-8',\n  timeout: 60000,\n});\n```\n\n**Why it fails:**\n- Working directory is `packages/daemon/`\n- `bun build --compile src/index.ts` resolves imports from this directory\n- Import `../../parser/index.js` tries to find `packages/parser/` (doesn't exist)\n- Compilation fails with unresolved imports\n\n**Why the test has commented notes:**\n```typescript\n// When running from packages/daemon, outfile is relative to that directory\n// But bun seems to resolve it from the repo root. Let's check both.\nconst possiblePaths = [\n  join(process.cwd(), 'dist/kspec-daemon'),           // Root dist\n  join(daemonDir, 'dist/kspec-daemon'),               // Daemon dist\n];\n```\n\nThis suggests developers have observed Bun's behavior is inconsistent or context-dependent.\n\n### Summary: The Full Picture\n\n| Component | Details |\n|-----------|---------|\n| **Package Structure** | Monorepo with `packages/{daemon,shared,web-ui}` + root `src/{parser,utils,cli,...}` |\n| **Entry Point** | `packages/daemon/src/index.ts` (with `#!/usr/bin/env bun`) |\n| **CLI Arguments** | `--port 3456` (default), `--kspec-dir .kspec` (default) |\n| **Server Framework** | Elysia.js with CORS, static serving, WebSocket support |\n| **Routes** | 5 route handlers (tasks, items, inbox, meta, validation) |\n| **Cross-Package Imports** | Routes use `../../parser/index.js`, `../../utils/grep.js` relative paths |\n| **Build Process** | `npm run build` → copies daemon sources to `dist/daemon/` → then `bun build --compile` |\n| **Standalone Binary** | `bun build --compile --minify src/index.ts --outfile dist/kspec-daemon` produces 100% standalone executable |\n| **PID Management** | `~/.config/kspec/daemon.{pid,port}` files for lifecycle control |\n| **Multi-Project** | ProjectContextManager handles X-Kspec-Dir header for multiple projects |\n| **WebSocket** | Pub/sub system broadcasts file changes and task updates per-project |\n| **Test Coverage** | `tests/daemon-executable.test.ts` validates compilation, permissions, and standalone execution |\n| **Known Issue** | Relative import paths fail when running `bun build --compile` from daemon package directory; requires running from project root |\n\n---\n\n## Absolute File Paths Referenced\n\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/package.json` (root)\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/daemon/package.json`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/daemon/tsconfig.json`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/daemon/src/index.ts`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/daemon/src/server.ts`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/daemon/src/pid.ts`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/daemon/src/project-context.ts`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/daemon/src/watcher.ts`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/daemon/src/middleware/project-context.ts`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/daemon/src/routes/tasks.ts`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/daemon/src/routes/items.ts`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/daemon/src/routes/meta.ts`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/daemon/src/routes/validation.ts`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/daemon/src/routes/inbox.ts`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/daemon/src/websocket/pubsub.ts`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/daemon/src/websocket/handler.ts`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/daemon/src/websocket/heartbeat.ts`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/daemon/src/websocket/types.ts`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/shared/package.json`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/scripts/build-executables.sh`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/tests/daemon-executable.test.ts`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/parser/index.ts` (exported from)\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/utils/grep.ts` (used in validation.ts)\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/dist/daemon/` (after build, contains TypeScript sources)"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a6c7e62 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 65415\ntool_uses: 29\nduration_ms: 86092</usage>"}]